  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Torch Technologies obligated $428M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Torch Technologies received 23 awards so far, with an average award size of $18.6M. Torch Technologies' obligations are down 37.7% year over year. Torch Technologies' multi-year record shows obligations of $470M in FY21, $589M in FY22, $674M in FY23, $629M in FY24, and $687M in FY25, before the current-year total of $428M. Torch Technologies concentrates its FY2026 obligations in research and engineering markets. Torch Technologies recorded $334M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) and $59.2M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology). Torch Technologies also reported $28.1M in Engineering Services, $4.5M in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing, and $2.1M in Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing. Torch Technologies' current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Torch Technologies' federal revenue trended over recent years?",
        "body": "Torch Technologies' obligations rose from $470M in FY21 to $674M in FY23, then dipped to $629M in FY24 and climbed to $687M in FY25. Torch Technologies' FY2026 to date obligations total $428M, down 37.7% year over year. Torch Technologies' current-year total is partial, covering the fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What contract markets and services drive Torch Technologies' obligations?",
        "body": "Research and development dominates Torch Technologies' FY2026 obligations, led by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) at $334M and a second R&D category at $59.2M. Torch Technologies also records Engineering Services at $28.1M, Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $4.5M, and Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $2.1M."
      }
    ]
